/-!
# Canonical OS complete joint Fréchet jet Banach-topology package

This aggregate root upgrades the scalar complete-jet sup gauges to the genuine
finite dependent-product norm topology after arbitrary finite-dimensional
compression. It exposes the normed and complete jet-space core, componentwise
and norm-topology `Tendsto` characterizations, joint continuity of complete and
rectangular carrier/response/trace jets, compact-uniform stability, arbitrary
joint-net closed-box stability, and diagonal no-rate stability for moving
finite direction families.

The canonical specialization remains strictly below the half-mass threshold
`G.mass / 2`, keeps the canonical OS Hilbert space infinite-dimensional, and
asserts operator-norm and trace convergence only after finite-dimensional
compression. No uncompressed operator norm, trace, complex spectral, Riesz
projection, root-convergence, or eigenvalue-enumeration claim is introduced.
-/
